<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Gramont</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gramont family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Gramont is a French noble family from the Basque borderland of Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, holding the castle and principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidache">Bidache</a>. Its members served as governors of Navarre and Béarn and as soldiers and courtiers of the French kings. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antoine-iii-de-gramont">Antoine III de Gramont</a> was a marshal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and was made a duke and peer in 1648, and the family's dukes of Gramont have continued into modern times.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-gramont.jpg" alt="House of Gramont" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_de_la_famille_de_Gramont.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
